  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Deloitte Consulting has $2.3B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Deloitte Consulting has 585 awards so far and an average award size of $4M. Obligations fell 22.1% year over year. Deloitte Consulting’s FY2026 obligations follow a multi-year sequence: $2.4B in FY21, $2.6B in FY22, $2.9B in FY23, $3.3B in FY24, $3B in FY25, and $2.3B in FY26. Deloitte Consulting’s largest single market is Computer Systems Design Services at $1.1B. Deloitte Consulting also has $515M in Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services and $248M in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology). The General Services Administration is Deloitte Consulting’s largest buyer in FY2026 to date at $656M. The Department of Defense, the Department of Veterans Affairs, and the Department of Health and Human Services follow with $354M, $350M, and $327M respectively.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 performance compare with prior years?",
        "body": "Deloitte Consulting’s FY2026 obligations are $2.3B, below the FY25 total of $3B and below the FY24 peak of $3.3B. Obligations have trended upward from FY21 through FY24 before declining in FY25 and falling 22.1% year over year into FY26. Deloitte Consulting’s award count for FY2026 to date is 585 with an average award size of $4M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Deloitte Consulting’s top federal customers and markets?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration is the top buyer in FY2026 to date at $656M, followed by the Department of Defense at $354M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $350M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market at $1.1B, with Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $515M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $248M."
      }
    ]
  },
